            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44307",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "mako: Mako: Information disclosure via directory traversal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Mako is a template library written in Python. Prior to 1.3.12, on Windows, a URI using backslash traversal (e.g. \\..\\..\\ secret.txt) bypasses the directory traversal check in Template.__init__ and the posixpath-based normalization in TemplateLookup.get_template(), allowing reads of files outside the configured template directory. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.3.12."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44307",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44307\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: Mako\nFixed Version: 1.3.12\nLink: [CVE-2026-44307](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44307)\nMako is a template library written in Python. Prior to 1.3.12, on Windows, a URI using backslash traversal (e.g. \\..\\..\\ secret.txt) bypasses the directory traversal check in Template.__init__ and the posixpath-based normalization in TemplateLookup.get_template(), allowing reads of files outside the configured template directory. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.3.12.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44307**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|Mako|1.3.12|[CVE-2026-44307](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44307)|\n\nMako is a template library written in Python. Prior to 1.3.12, on Windows, a URI using backslash traversal (e.g. \\..\\..\\ secret.txt) bypasses the directory traversal check in Template.__init__ and the posixpath-based normalization in TemplateLookup.get_template(), allowing reads of files outside the configured template directory. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.3.12."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 8.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-34993",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "aiohttp: AIOHTTP: Arbitrary code execution via untrusted input to CookieJar.load()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "AIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to version 3.14.0, using ``CookieJar.load()`` with untrusted input may allow arbitrary code execution. Most applications using this function will be doing so with the user's own data, so this is unlikely to affect many applications. Version 3.14.0 patches the issue. If an application does allow attacker controlled files to be loaded, a workaround on older releases would be to sanitize the files before loading."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34993",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-34993\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: aiohttp\nFixed Version: 3.14.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-34993](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34993)\nAIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to version 3.14.0, using ``CookieJar.load()`` with untrusted input may allow arbitrary code execution. Most applications using this function will be doing so with the user's own data, so this is unlikely to affect many applications. Version 3.14.0 patches the issue. If an application does allow attacker controlled files to be loaded, a workaround on older releases would be to sanitize the files before loading.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-34993**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|aiohttp|3.14.0|[CVE-2026-34993](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34993)|\n\nAIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to version 3.14.0, using ``CookieJar.load()`` with untrusted input may allow arbitrary code execution. Most applications using this function will be doing so with the user's own data, so this is unlikely to affect many applications. Version 3.14.0 patches the issue. If an application does allow attacker controlled files to be loaded, a workaround on older releases would be to sanitize the files before loading."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.4,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:H/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
